  "sourceData": {
    "answer": "to: cross-over/go-across | extend/cover/range/span",
    "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an <ja>う</ja> sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means <kanji>transit</kanji>, but when you think about \"to transit\" this doesn't make too much sense. When you \"transit\" something, though, you're going across it. That's why this word is <vocabulary>to cross</vocabulary> or <vocabulary>to cross over</vocabulary>.",
